{"name":"Quail Egg","hex":"#e3ddce","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"quail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To waste away; to fade, to wither. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To daunt or frighten (someone)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various small game birds of the genera Coturnix, Anurophasis or Perdicula in the Old World family Phasianidae or of the New World family Odontophoridae.","The meat from this bird eaten as food."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quail"},{"term":"egg","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food.","An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, reptiles, and other animals, often housing an embryo within a membrane or shell during its development.\n\n  The (usually) non-developing, edible egg (sense 1.1) of a domestic fowl such as a duck, goose, or, especially, chicken;  the contents of such an egg or eggs used as food."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something).","To throw (especially rotten) eggs (noun sense 1.1.1) at (someone or something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/egg"}],"entries":[{"title":"Quail eggs","blocks":[{"text":"Quail eggs are the eggs of quails, which are edible and widely considered a delicacy. As quails has already been farmed extensively for long, their eggs has also been always readily available and consumed across the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Potato_galettes_with_quail_eggs.jpg/330px-Potato_galettes_with_quail_eggs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quail_eggs"},{"title":"Quail","blocks":[{"text":"Quail is a collective name for several genera of mid-sized birds generally placed in the order Galliformes. The collective noun for a group of quail is a flock, covey, or bevy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Brown_Quail.jpg/330px-Brown_Quail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quail"},{"title":"Egg","blocks":[{"text":"An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has developed enough to survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/330px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/QuailChickenDuckEggsinHand.JPG/500px-QuailChickenDuckEggsinHand.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/QuailChickenDuckEggsinHand.JPG/1280px-QuailChickenDuckEggsinHand.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/QuailChickenDuckEggsinHand.JPG/500px-QuailChickenDuckEggsinHand.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Quail egg (left) as compared to a chicken egg (upper right) and a duck egg (lower right) (the quail egg being the smallest), in an adult human's hand",